      ":question/id": "c90cd801-8b18-54b6-8ab2-396380c16785",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $4P-\\frac{1}{2}H$, where\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nand\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$H=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$4P-\\frac{1}{2}H=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We multiply each entry of $P$ by $4$ and each entry of $H$ by $\\frac{1}{2},$ and then subtract the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4P-\\frac{1}{2}H & =4\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\cdot 4 & 4\\cdot (-3) & 4\\cdot 1 & 4\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 & -12 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}16-2 & -12-2 & 4-1 & 0-0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}14 & -14 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    }
  ],
