      ":question/difficulty": {
        ":db/id": 17592186045487
      },
      ":question/id": "1b043b81-1ada-5815-850e-33b61f29ebfb",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 8 & -8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 2 & -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $P$ is a $1\\times 2$ row vector, $R$ is a $1\\times 2$ row vector, and $S$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $R$ and $2$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $P$ and $1$ row in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $P$ and $2$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $P$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe products $RS$ and $PS$ are well defined. The product $PR$ is undefined."
    }
  ],
