      },
      ":question/id": "a9443487-659f-5f55-805a-f53e518e3e7d",
      ":question/problem": "Let\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhat are the dimensions of $SR$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We notice that $S$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $R$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $S$ and $1$ row in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $SR$ has dimensions $2\\times 2:$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={SR}_{2\\times 2}\n$$"
